1
00:01:57,915 --> 00:01:59,915


2
00:01:59,939 --> 00:02:04,680
Now, before we begin today's story, let us recap last week's events.

3
00:02:05,446 --> 00:02:07,571
One night, the King went missing and was presumed dead,


4
00:02:07,595 --> 00:02:12,700
so Sapphire was set
to ascend the throne.

5
00:02:13,429 --> 00:02:14,176
However,

6
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,018
amid the grand celebration, the Queen fell victim to the evil scheme of

7
00:02:17,042 --> 00:02:21,700
Grand Duke Duralumin and Lord Nylon
and was tricked into drinking poison.

8
00:02:22,265 --> 00:02:23,265
Oh no!

9
00:02:23,555 --> 00:02:27,660
This poison forces whoever drinks it to reveal all the secrets in their heart.

10
00:02:28,336 --> 00:02:28,989
Oh how lovely!

11
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,531
In front of the kingdom's representatives and

12
00:02:30,555 --> 00:02:33,885
foreign dignitaries, the Queen blabbed Sapphire's secret—

13
00:02:33,909 --> 00:02:40,480
yes, the secret that Sapphire is actually a girl, not a boy.

14
00:02:41,163 --> 00:02:44,698
For the crime of deceiving the people, Sapphire and the Queen 

15
00:02:44,722 --> 00:02:46,658
were sentenced to life imprisonment
in

16
00:02:46,682 --> 00:02:49,786
the terrifying prison known as the Coffin Tower.

17
00:02:52,404 --> 00:02:56,900
What fate lies in store for Sapphire and the Queen?

18
00:02:57,385 --> 00:03:00,440
Please enjoy today's episode.

19
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,340
Gama, jailer of the tower! Are you there?

20
00:03:39,484 --> 00:03:41,860
Yes, right away, Captain!

21
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:58,660
Mother.

22
00:03:58,684 --> 00:04:00,540
Stay strong... Hang in there, Sapphire.

23
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,520
Let Sapphire and the Queen out.

24
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:07,247
Mother, be careful.

25
00:04:07,271 --> 00:04:08,320
Thank you, Sapphire.

26
00:04:10,695 --> 00:04:13,953
Welcome, Prince Sapphire and the Queen.

27
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:17,853
Gama, I leave them in your care.

28
00:04:18,019 --> 00:04:18,426
Let's go!

29
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,540
Y-Yes, sir. Thank you for your hard work.

30
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,080
Now, shall we?

31
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:43,240
Oh, what a dreadful tower this is.

32
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,960
Right this way, please.

33
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,220
What was that noise, Gama?

34
00:04:58,690 --> 00:04:59,540
Just the wind.

35
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,853
If that frightens you, you won't last long in the Coffin Tower.

36
00:05:03,715 --> 00:05:04,860
Where is our room?

37
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:09,033
Yes, just up those stairs.

38
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:25,634
Sapphire, bats!

39
00:05:25,658 --> 00:05:26,725
Oh, that scared me.

40
00:05:27,015 --> 00:05:28,400
There sure are all kinds of things in here.

41
00:05:28,424 --> 00:05:29,720
Here we are.

42
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:34,740
This is the room for the two of you.

43
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:41,120
Are there no beds in this room?

44
00:05:41,606 --> 00:05:42,040
Beds?

45
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:44,840
Men, get two beds ready!

46
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,300
Who are these people?

47
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,040
They're all my men.

48
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:53,160
Give me that jewel in exchange for beds.

49
00:05:53,375 --> 00:05:56,773
Oh, but this is a precious keepsake of the King...

50
00:05:57,585 --> 00:05:59,473
Hey, looks like they don't need beds after all.

51
00:06:02,890 --> 00:06:05,426
Huddle up and sleep on the stones, then.

52
00:06:06,003 --> 00:06:06,647
Gama— 

53
00:06:06,671 --> 00:06:07,674
Sapphire,

54
00:06:07,698 --> 00:06:08,640
Mother...

55
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:09,826
It's all right.

56
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,713
Men, bring in the beds!

57
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,280
Could we have some light in the room?

58
00:06:19,225 --> 00:06:21,120
Men, bring a light!

59
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:27,100
In payment for the candles, give me that brooch.

60
00:06:27,670 --> 00:06:28,670
What?!

61
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:30,526
Enough of your greed!

62
00:06:30,730 --> 00:06:32,620
Hey, looks like they don't need light after all.

63
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,100
Ah, wait!

64
00:06:36,305 --> 00:06:37,305
We have no choice...

65
00:06:48,930 --> 00:06:50,820
It's already been three days since we came here.

66
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:52,940
Sapphire, you must be hungry.

67
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:57,266
We haven't eaten anything since breakfast.

68
00:06:58,450 --> 00:07:00,793
What should I do about dinner?

69
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:05,880
I'd like some, but we've run out of necklaces and rings.

70
00:07:06,315 --> 00:07:09,293
Well, you two still have those fine clothes.

71
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:12,640
If I give you these, could we get something else to wear?

72
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,180
Of course. Something very fine.

73
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:18,980
Mother...

74
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:20,110
It's all right.

75
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,800
Oh, Mother... wearing clothes like that...

76
00:07:26,005 --> 00:07:29,580
No, we have no need for fine dresses anymore.

77
00:07:30,695 --> 00:07:36,893
Hey, food's ready! Come on. Goodness, trading our fine clothes for only this?

78
00:07:37,150 --> 00:07:39,900
I wish I could at least let Sapphire eat her fill.

79
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:43,580
That'll take a few more jewels or something.

80
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:45,760
But I have nothing left.

81
00:07:46,625 --> 00:07:48,346
Are you hiding something?

82
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:50,940
No, really, it's nothing.

83
00:07:51,205 --> 00:07:53,093
There's nothing here. Nothing at all.

84
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,220
Then the mother does the laundry, and the kid cleans the house!

85
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:56,880
What?

86
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,300
Making Mother work?!

87
00:07:59,318 --> 00:08:00,620
Oh, Sapphire.

88
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:05,913
I'm gonna work you two to the bone today!

89
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:11,500
Aren't we energetic...

90
00:08:11,985 --> 00:08:14,413
Gama's cruelty doesn't bother me at all.

91
00:08:19,195 --> 00:08:21,940
I'd rather work than sit around moping.

92
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,580
Honestly, keeping busy makes me feel better.

93
00:08:26,765 --> 00:08:27,460
Gama!

94
00:08:27,484 --> 00:08:28,374
You washed my face!

95
00:08:29,639 --> 00:08:30,480
Ouch!

96
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,080
Less talking, more working!

97
00:08:44,959 --> 00:08:48,993
Getting hit and then stuck with trash duty? Give me a break.

98
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:52,900
Let's see, the trash dump is... Ah, right here.

99
00:09:03,549 --> 00:09:04,796
Hey! Who's there?!

100
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,880
Damn, this was Gama's room.

101
00:09:09,819 --> 00:09:14,199
Damn it! Make a fool of Master Gama again, and you won't get off easy!

102
00:09:14,265 --> 00:09:16,819
I didn't know it was your room, Gama!

103
00:09:16,975 --> 00:09:18,353
No food for you!

104
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,893
Scrub the floor.

105
00:09:20,130 --> 00:09:21,580
Now that you get it...

106
00:09:28,059 --> 00:09:29,059
I get it!

107
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:32,306
Let's see, a rag, a rag...

108
00:09:32,330 --> 00:09:33,361
Ah, this one!

109
00:09:36,685 --> 00:09:37,665
♪ la la la ♪
-

110
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:39,552
♪ la la la ♪
-

111
00:09:40,638 --> 00:09:44,605
♪ la la lan la lan la lan lan lan lan ♪
-

112
00:09:44,803 --> 00:09:51,963
♪ Sonochi harema ga mierudaro ♪
One of these days we'll see some sunshine

113
00:09:52,429 --> 00:09:53,483
♪ la la la ♪
-

114
00:09:54,583 --> 00:09:55,529
♪ la la la ♪
-

115
00:09:56,623 --> 00:09:59,863
♪ la la la la lan lan lan ♪
-

116
00:10:01,246 --> 00:10:08,406
♪ Sonochi minna ga utaudaro ♪
One of these days we'll all be singing

117
00:10:08,509 --> 00:10:09,815
♪ la la la ♪
-

118
00:10:10,429 --> 00:10:12,069
♪ la la la ♪
-

119
00:10:12,589 --> 00:10:15,782
♪ la la la la lan lan lan ♪
-

120
00:10:16,366 --> 00:10:24,366
♪ Sonochi harema ga mierudaro ♪
One of these days we'll see some sunshine

121
00:10:24,575 --> 00:10:25,542
♪ la la la ♪
-

122
00:10:26,455 --> 00:10:27,602
♪ la la la ♪
-

123
00:10:28,549 --> 00:10:31,922
♪ la la la la lan lan lan ♪
-

124
00:10:37,435 --> 00:10:39,453
What kind of floor-wiping is that?

125
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,326
Give it here!

126
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:43,099
I can't put my back into it unless I sing to the beat!

127
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:45,390
That is one filthy rag...

128
00:10:48,583 --> 00:10:49,009
H-Hey!

129
00:10:49,430 --> 00:10:50,676
Those are my clothes!

130
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,373
Oh, these are your clothes Gama?!

131
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:53,880
Wait!

132
00:11:07,609 --> 00:11:08,880
Oh no, the cook!

133
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:10,206
My food...

134
00:11:13,765 --> 00:11:15,740
What an infuriating brat!

135
00:11:15,905 --> 00:11:19,073
No way, you're going to keep working with no food for a long time!

136
00:11:19,185 --> 00:11:20,313
Now keep at it!

137
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:36,557
<i>Soon the sun</i>...

138
00:11:36,581 --> 00:11:38,293
Stop singing!

139
00:11:38,525 --> 00:11:40,006
Grind fine flour!

140
00:11:40,335 --> 00:11:43,900
So Master Gama can eat top-quality bread baked from it!

141
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:45,339
Oh, no you don't!

142
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:49,700
A mouse!

143
00:11:50,186 --> 00:11:50,426
Wait!

144
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:51,920
You thieving mouse!

145
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:10,380
Hand it over!

146
00:12:16,449 --> 00:12:20,080
Starting today, we're ridding this mansion of these filthy mice!

147
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,026
No!

148
00:12:21,245 --> 00:12:22,520
Mice are living creatures, too!

149
00:12:34,016 --> 00:12:35,319
I'm so hungry...

150
00:12:35,577 --> 00:12:38,566
Tomorrow I'll give you my share.

151
00:12:39,410 --> 00:12:40,566
I'm happy...

152
00:12:41,097 --> 00:12:42,241
Why?

153
00:12:42,719 --> 00:12:46,413
Because even though things are tough, it's just the two of us, Mother.

154
00:12:47,184 --> 00:12:50,499
Truly... If only your father were here...

155
00:12:50,523 --> 00:12:52,461
We promised not to cry!

156
00:12:54,129 --> 00:12:54,993
I'm sorry... 

157
00:12:55,237 --> 00:12:57,446
We don't need annoying etiquette,

158
00:12:58,343 --> 00:13:00,579
and creepy Duralumin and Nylon aren't here either...

159
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:01,659
This place...

160
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:04,013
isn't so bad after all.

161
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:05,380
Thank you, Sapphire.

162
00:13:05,975 --> 00:13:08,680
Looking at your face gives me courage, too.

163
00:13:09,729 --> 00:13:14,026
But still... I'm so hungry...

164
00:13:21,705 --> 00:13:23,200
Did you come to thank us?

165
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,066
You didn't have to!

166
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,213
I'm so touched!

167
00:13:30,539 --> 00:13:32,446
You brought food as a thank-you!

168
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,480
Well then!

169
00:13:37,915 --> 00:13:38,915
It's delicious!

170
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:40,050
Here's another!

171
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,140
Hey!

172
00:13:42,459 --> 00:13:45,380
From now on, no one is to speak of Prince Sapphire.

173
00:13:45,725 --> 00:13:49,186
Anyone who utters the name... will be whipped over a hundred times

174
00:13:49,210 --> 00:13:51,700
and sent to the quarry as a slave, Lord Duralumin!

175
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,360
That wretched Duralumin!

176
00:13:53,514 --> 00:13:55,180
They're running things terribly, Mother!

177
00:13:57,399 --> 00:13:58,660
I'm sure that's not all!

178
00:13:59,350 --> 00:14:03,693


179
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:08,280
If only we could get out of here...

180
00:14:10,165 --> 00:14:12,200
What is this...?

181
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,160
Mother!

182
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:21,980
What kind of hole is this?

183
00:14:25,735 --> 00:14:29,976
It's deep... It might go all the way down... 

184
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,440
Be careful, it's very narrow.

185
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,100
It's the outside!

186
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:12,640
We can get outside, little mouse!

187
00:15:13,186 --> 00:15:13,986
Thank you!

188
00:15:24,109 --> 00:15:25,423
Ah, Sapphire!

189
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:27,420
Mother, there's an exit!

190
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,200
Come on, hurry and climb up... Let's get out of here!

191
00:15:30,474 --> 00:15:32,300
We're escaping from this place right now!

192
00:15:32,805 --> 00:15:34,920
I can't fit through a hole this small.

193
00:15:35,085 --> 00:15:36,380
You must escape alone.

194
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:37,686
No!

195
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:39,360
I won't leave you, Mother...

196
00:15:40,170 --> 00:15:42,240
No, you must escape, even if it's just you.

197
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:44,500
And fight the villains.

198
00:15:47,479 --> 00:15:48,780
Stay strong...

199
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,946
What are you whispering about over there?

200
00:15:53,514 --> 00:15:57,294
Nothing... Ah, I'm so hungry.

201
00:15:57,319 --> 00:16:01,220
Starving... You were probably plotting an escape anyway.

202
00:16:01,395 --> 00:16:02,560
As if you could escape!

203
00:16:02,930 --> 00:16:07,100
If you run, the Queen loses her head in your place!

204
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:11,400
On Lord Duralumin's orders!

205
00:16:13,079 --> 00:16:14,420
Mother...

206
00:16:15,055 --> 00:16:16,100
Don't worry about me.

207
00:16:16,795 --> 00:16:18,580
Get out of here and fight.

208
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,180
That is the duty of the Prince of Silverland.

209
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:32,860
But if I'm caught, your life... Sapphire, which is more important? My life, or the lives of all the poor people suffering at the hands of villains?

210
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:40,300
Oh, a mouse!

211
00:16:45,385 --> 00:16:48,120
Wow, my sword and clothes!

212
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:50,260
You brought them from the Chamber of Patience!

213
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,819
Mother... Come on, keep moving!

214
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:19,460
Flogging!

215
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:20,300
Flogging!

216
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,640
Flogging!

217
00:17:24,175 --> 00:17:25,540
Listen up, everyone!

218
00:17:25,639 --> 00:17:30,780
Not only did this man speak Sapphire's name, he had the nerve to call King Plastic a fool!

219
00:17:31,179 --> 00:17:35,560
So after a good flogging, we'll send him to the quarry and work him as a slave until he dies!

220
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:45,220
No!

221
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:46,960
No, no, no, no, no!

222
00:17:46,961 --> 00:17:49,140
This brat was praising Sapphire!

223
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:50,020
What?

224
00:17:50,619 --> 00:17:54,980
Dad, King Plastic kept Sapphire alive, but now he's gone completely mad!

225
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,800
You little runt! Whip him!

226
00:17:58,139 --> 00:17:59,860
Don't hold back just because he's a kid! Get him!

227
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:03,860
My little boy!

228
00:18:04,899 --> 00:18:06,990
They're just the words of a child. Please forgive him.

229
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:07,960
No! Absolutely not!

230
00:18:08,079 --> 00:18:09,860
Move, or I'll whip both of you!

231
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,200
There!

232
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,300
Wait!

233
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:41,340
Here we go!

234
00:18:41,409 --> 00:18:42,580
Who are you?!

235
00:18:44,625 --> 00:18:45,625
Princess Knight!

236
00:18:46,110 --> 00:18:47,110
Remember it!

237
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:47,880
What?

238
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,040
"Princess Knight"?

239
00:18:49,994 --> 00:18:51,160
A strange heartbeat!

240
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:52,260
You lone monkey!

241
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,160
What's wrong?

242
00:19:02,459 --> 00:19:03,480
Is that all you've got?

243
00:19:03,924 --> 00:19:05,760
So much for your whip tricks!

244
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,160
Come on!

245
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,020
Thanks!

246
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,300
Boy!

247
00:19:31,779 --> 00:19:34,900
Use this sword to cut the prisoner's ropes in the carriage!

248
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:37,220
Thank you, Princess Knight!

249
00:19:37,484 --> 00:19:40,140
Um, please, at least show us your face!

250
00:19:41,045 --> 00:19:42,320
I cannot do that!

251
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,560
Farewell!

252
00:20:03,079 --> 00:20:04,580
Princess Knight, we've got trouble!

253
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,080
We've got trouble!

254
00:20:10,409 --> 00:20:11,500
How ridiculous!

255
00:20:11,834 --> 00:20:13,360
Are you hungry?

256
00:20:14,659 --> 00:20:16,100
You don't even care how I feel!

257
00:20:16,329 --> 00:20:17,680
You idiot, Plastic!

258
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:19,360
What's wrong?

259
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:23,160
Ugh, it's so frustrating!

260
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:23,760
What do you mean, "what"?!

261
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:28,480
Some weirdo suddenly showed up and freed all the prisoners bound for the quarry!

262
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,320
Strange?

263
00:20:31,144 --> 00:20:32,740
What do you mean, "strange"?!

264
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:38,821
That monster was a giant three meters tall, and he almost had us beat, but then... Little Ribbon!

265
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,160
Yikes, he's here!

266
00:20:41,779 --> 00:20:42,820
That's him! Right there!

267
00:20:43,935 --> 00:20:46,520
The reason he's weird is... Guards!

268
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:47,160
Guards!

269
00:20:47,529 --> 00:20:48,940
There's an intruder at the window!

270
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,840
Attack from all sides! Secure the outside of the window, too!

271
00:20:51,985 --> 00:20:53,280
Cut off his escape route!

272
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,240
Pardon the intrusion!

273
00:20:55,395 --> 00:20:57,740
Put your hands up, or we'll turn you into a honeycomb!

274
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,440
Ouch!

275
00:20:58,700 --> 00:20:59,140
Ouch!

276
00:20:59,141 --> 00:21:00,141
Duralumin!

277
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:10,100
The fat guy must be the main target!

278
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:11,180
Let's wreck this place!

279
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:11,680
Take that!

280
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,140
Quick, catch him!

281
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,720
Don't you forget it!

282
00:21:18,784 --> 00:21:20,580
You greedy, cunning Duralumin!

283
00:21:20,899 --> 00:21:24,740
If you keep harassing the people, the Ribbon Knight won't stand for it!

284
00:21:25,205 --> 00:21:26,205
Remember that!

285
00:21:28,599 --> 00:21:29,760
What are you doing?!

286
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:30,100
After him!

287
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,200
Get him!

288
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,180
What is it, Nylon?

289
00:21:35,374 --> 00:21:38,620
That voice sounded an awful lot like Sapphire's.

290
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:39,860
What?

291
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Sapphire?

292
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:42,900
That's it!

293
00:21:43,149 --> 00:21:44,500
First, split into two groups!

294
00:21:44,725 --> 00:21:46,280
One group will chase that monster!

295
00:21:46,444 --> 00:21:49,820
The other will go to Kagoge Island to see if Sapphire is there!

296
00:21:50,595 --> 00:21:51,595
What?

297
00:21:51,779 --> 00:21:55,260
The Ribbon Knight is... Sapphire?!

298
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:26,940
Oh no!

299
00:22:27,414 --> 00:22:30,640
Nylon caught on and is heading to Kagoge Island ahead of us to check!

300
00:22:31,064 --> 00:22:32,600
If I don't hurry back, Mother will be in danger!

301
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:47,400
Gama!

302
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:48,600
Is Gama there?

303
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:49,180
It's Nylon!

304
00:22:49,465 --> 00:22:50,465
Open the tower immediately!

305
00:22:52,894 --> 00:22:53,894
Ouch!

306
00:23:02,499 --> 00:23:03,499
Hello, Nylon!

307
00:23:03,649 --> 00:23:05,240
Your nose is as big as ever!

308
00:23:05,325 --> 00:23:07,180
I was so sure it was Sapphire...

309
00:23:10,304 --> 00:23:11,940
I'm sorry I'm late.

310
00:23:12,605 --> 00:23:13,605
What a relief.

311
00:23:14,064 --> 00:23:16,980
If you were any later, it would have been dangerous.

312
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,560
So much sweat...

313
00:23:23,559 --> 00:23:26,800
So was Sapphire really inside the tower?

314
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:27,040
Yes.

315
00:23:27,379 --> 00:23:31,680
We're stuck going through all this trouble because Sapphire and the Queen are still alive.

316
00:23:31,935 --> 00:23:33,080
Damn it!

317
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:36,660
Finish them quickly... I've already made my move!

318
00:23:37,234 --> 00:23:39,960
I hired a hitman who uses three different weapons!

319
00:23:41,434 --> 00:23:43,420
They should be at the tower by now!

320
00:23:43,980 --> 00:23:44,980
What?

321
00:23:47,929 --> 00:23:49,400
How good is this assassin?

322
00:23:49,949 --> 00:23:54,000
He's never failed before. Just watch.

323
00:23:54,024 --> 00:23:56,024

